.TH SDL_SetGPUAllowedFramesInFlight 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetGPUAllowedFramesInFlight \- Configures the maximum allowed number of frames in flight.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetGPUAllowedFramesInFlight(
.BI "    SDL_GPUDevice *device,
.BI "    Uint32 allowed_frames_in_flight);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The default value when the device is created is 2\[char46] This means that after you have submitted 2 frames for presentation, if the GPU has not finished working on the first frame,
.BR SDL_AcquireGPUSwapchainTexture ()
will fill the swapchain texture pointer with NULL, and
.BR SDL_WaitAndAcquireGPUSwapchainTexture ()
will block\[char46]
.PP
Higher values increase throughput at the expense of visual latency\[char46] Lower values decrease visual latency at the expense of throughput\[char46]
.PP
Note that calling this function will stall and flush the command queue to prevent synchronization issues\[char46]
.PP
The minimum value of allowed frames in flight is 1, and the maximum is 3\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I device
a GPU context\[char46]
.TP
.I allowed_frames_in_flight
the maximum number of frames that can be pending on the GPU\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if successful, false on error; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

